!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! FORMAT !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\
\
!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\
!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! Bimolecular reactions !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\
!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\
The format of the reactions_1.dat file (Bimolecular reactions) is the following :\
\
Format : 3(1x,a10) 3(1x,a10) 5(1x,e10.3)\
Reactants  Products  Alpha  Beta  Gamma  F g\
\
Alpha, Beta, Gamma are the parameters to compute the rate coefficients. The formula adopted follows the Kooij formalism.\
(See http:// kida.obs.u-bordeaux1.fr/help).\
\
F is the uncertainty factor on the rate coefficient (See http://kida.obs.u-bordeaux1.fr/help)\
\
g is the temperature dependence of this uncertainty factor (See http://kida.obs.u-bordeaux1.fr/help)\
\
Type of uncertainty is lognormal (logn)\
\
!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\
!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! Termolecular reactions !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\
!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\
The format of the reactions_2.dat file (Termolecular reactions) is the following :\
\
Format : 3(1x,a10) 3(1x,a10) 10(1x,e10.3)\
Reactants  Products  Alpha_0  Beta_0  Gamma_0  F_0  g_0 Alpha_inf  Beta_inf  Gamma_inf  F_inf  g_inf\
\
Alpha_0, Beta_0, Gamma_0 and Alpha_inf, Beta_inf,, Gamma_inf,  are the parameters to compute the rate coefficients k_0 and k_inf, respectively. The formula adopted follows the Kooij and Troe formalisms.\
(See http:// kida.obs.u-bordeaux1.fr/help).\
\
F is the uncertainty factor on the specific rate coefficient considered (See http://kida.obs.u-bordeaux1.fr/help).\
\
g is the temperature dependence of this uncertainty factor (See http://kida.obs.u-bordeaux1.fr/help).\
\
Type of uncertainty is lognormal (logn).\
\
!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\
!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! Adduct stabilizations !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\
!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\
Adduct stabilization A + B 
\f1 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  C designates the conjugation of the termolecular reaction A + B + M 
\f1 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  C + M and the radiative association A + B 
\f1 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  C + h\uc0\u957 . \
\
The format of the reactions_3.dat file (Adduct stabilizations) is the following :\
\
Format : 3(1x,a10) 3(1x,a10) 15(1x,e10.3)\
Reactants  Products  Alpha_0  Beta_0  Gamma_0  F_0  g_0 Alpha_inf  Beta_inf  Gamma_inf  F_inf  g_inf  Alpha_r  Beta_r  Gamma_r  F_r  g_r\
\
Alpha_0, Beta_0, Gamma_0 and Alpha_inf, Beta_inf,, Gamma_inf and Alpha_r, Beta_r, Gamma_r are the parameters to compute the rate coefficients k_0, k_inf, and k_r respectively. The formula adopted follow the Kooij formalism. Adduct stabilization rate coefficient k_adduct is calculated from a modified Troe formalism, adjusted to include radiative associations.\
\
F is the uncertainty factor on the specific rate coefficient considered (See http://kida.obs.u-bordeaux1.fr/help).\
\
g is the temperature dependence of this uncertainty factor (See http://kida.obs.u-bordeaux1.fr/help).\
\
Type of uncertainty is lognormal (logn).\
\
!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\
!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! Bimolecular reactions / Adduct stabilizations !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\
!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\
Bimolecular products formation competes with adduct stabilization when occuring through addition.\
\
The format of the reactions_4.dat file (Bimolecular reactions / Adduct stabilizations) is the following :\
\
Format : 3(1x,a10) 3(1x,a10) 16(1x,e10.3)\
Reactants  Products  factor  Alpha_0  Beta_0  Gamma_0  F_0  g_0 Alpha_inf  Beta_inf  Gamma_inf  F_inf  g_inf  Alpha_r  Beta_r  Gamma_r  F_r  g_r\
\
Adduct stabilization is listed first.\
Alpha_0, Beta_0, Gamma_0 and Alpha_inf, Beta_inf,, Gamma_inf and Alpha_r, Beta_r, Gamma_r are the parameters to compute the rate coefficients\
k_0, k_inf, and k_r respectively. The formula adopted follow the Kooij formalism. Adduct stabilization rate coefficient k_adduct is calculated from a modified Troe formalism, adjusted to include radiative associations.\
\
Bimolecular rate coefficient k_bimo is calculated by considering that the total rate coefficient is  constant, leading to k_bimo = facteur*(k_inf \uc0\u8722  k_adduct).\
\
F is the uncertainty factor on the specific rate coefficient considered (See http://kida.obs.u-bordeaux1.fr/help).\
\
g is the temperature dependence of this uncertainty factor (See http://kida.obs.u-bordeaux1.fr/help).\
\
Type of uncertainty is lognormal (logn).\
\
